# Wildcards — `? super T` & PECS

## `? super T` — a lower bound

`List<? super Integer>` = Integer or a supertype. The trade-off **flips**:

```java
void addNumbers(List<? super Integer> dest) {
    dest.add(1);              // ✅ an Integer always fits
    Object o = dest.get(0);   // read only as Object
    Integer i = dest.get(0);  // ❌ could be List<Number>
}
```

Model: a **consumer** — data flows **in**.

## PECS — Producer `extends`, Consumer `super`

- Parameter **produces** `T`s you read → `? extends T`
- Parameter **consumes** `T`s you supply → `? super T`
- **Both** → exact `List<T>`, no wildcard

```java
static <T> void copy(List<? super T> dest, List<? extends T> src) {
    for (T x : src) dest.add(x);   // src produces, dest consumes
}
```

## Seen everywhere

`Collections.max(… ? extends T)` · `forEach(Consumer<? super T>)` · `Comparator<? super T>` · `map(Function<? super T, ? extends R>)`
